    "RUNG FOUND AT AND CURRENT RUNG: silent acceptance on interpretation -- outside the ladder for the compile-time class; the runtime witness comparison is the rung-1 mitigation. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The identity of a bare marker declaration is a declaration identity the namespace tree already carries, and the checker demonstrably refuses a kernel-primitive mismatch at the same position (TypeMismatch|Primitive(String) in the same run), so there is no undecidability here, only an unjudged position.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, capability grain: a declaration-identity judgment at generic ARGUMENT positions that compares each bound type argument's resolved declaration against the formal's, refusing a distinct-marker pair and admitting an identical one, on the interpretation path. Sufficient for flipping the enrolled probe to ExpectBlockingRefusal and deleting the runtime CategoryDisagreesWithSink arm's role as the only wall (the arm stays as the executed evidence). Not satisfied by an emit-side rendering witness, and not by the sibling unit-variant repair unless it also covers bare declarations.",
